module j3.memory

struct List<T>
    Growable contiguous list backed by an arena (old buffers are abandoned, not freed).
    at j3/memory.j3:241 (embedded in j3c)
    items: []T
        Storage slice (length is capacity).
    len: int
        Number of live elements.
    arena: &Arena
        Arena used for reallocation.
    fn List<T>.new(arena: &Arena): List<T>
        Empty list allocated from `arena`.
    fn List<T>.push(this: &List<T>, item: T)
        Append `item`, doubling capacity from 0→4 then ×2 as needed.
    fn List<T>.remove(this: &List<T>, i: int)
        Remove element `i`, keeping the order of the rest. Out of range is a no-op.
    fn List<T>.swapRemove(this: &List<T>, i: int)
        Remove element `i` by moving the last element into its place (O(1), order changes).
    fn List<T>.reserve(this: &List<T>, n: int)
        Room for at least `n` elements without another reallocation.
    fn List<T>.pop(this: &List<T>): T
        Remove and return the last element; panics when empty.
    fn List<T>.last(this: &List<T>): T
        The last element; panics when empty.
    fn List<T>.insert(this: &List<T>, i: int, item: T)
        Put `item` at index `i` (0..=len), moving the rest up one. Panics when `i` is out of range.
    fn List<T>.clear(this: &List<T>)
        Drop every element, keeping the storage.
    fn List<T>.extend(this: &List<T>, xs: []T)
        Append every element of `xs`.
    fn List<T>.slice(this: &List<T>): []T
        The live elements as a slice (`items[0..len]`); valid until the next growth.
    fn List<T>.indexOf(this: &List<T>, x: T): int
        Index of the first element equal to `x`, or -1. Needs `T: Eq` (its `where`), checked where it
        is called, so a `List` of a type without `==` is fine as long as nothing calls this.
    fn List<T>.contains(this: &List<T>, x: T): bool
        True when some element equals `x` (`T: Eq`, like `indexOf`).

